Description: firewalld manager for the Trinity Desktop Environment [Trinity]
 tde-firewalld is a graphical front end for firewalld, the dynamic firewall
 daemon. It is available both as a Trinity Control Center module
 (Security & Privacy > Firewall) and as a standalone application.
 .
 It shows the firewall state and active zones, and lets you change the
 default zone, allow services and ports, configure masquerading, port
 forwarding and rich rules, and bind interfaces and sources to zones, in
 either the runtime or the permanent configuration.
 .
 It communicates with firewalld over D-Bus; privileged operations are
 authorized by polkit through polkit-agent-tde.
